Parity arithmetic reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity, NOT a
"corrected" version):
  vehicleCount  = vehicles?.length ?? 0                         → rendered RAW (React {n} → String(n),
  onlineCount   = vehicles.filter(state=='online').length ?? 0    NO grouping separators)
  totalDistance = convertDistanceFromSI(analytics.total_distance_km ?? 0, distancePref)
                  [ /1000 km · /1609.344 mi · /0.3048 ft ]  ← NB: km value fed in DIRECTLY,
                  NO `* KM_TO_MI` pre-multiply (this differs from LifetimeStatsWidget; verbatim port).
  totalEnergy   = analytics.total_energy_kwh ?? 0
  distance/energy value = fmtNumber(v, 1)  (en_US grouped, 1 fraction digit, half-away-from-zero)
  onlinePct     = vehicleCount>0 ? `${fmtNumber(online/vehicleCount*100, 0)}%` : undefined
  hasData       = (vehicles && vehicles.length>0) || analytics   (else → friendly empty state)

Composition parity note (StatCard trend): the web items set `trendValue` but NOT a `trend`
DIRECTION, and `WidgetStatGrid`→`StatCard` renders a trend row ONLY when a direction is present
(verified against the web StatCard + the native predecessor MileageStatTile). So the web renders
four plain tiles (label/value/unit/icon) — reproduced exactly (strict visual parity, no drift).
The computed online count + percent (the suppressed `trendValue`s) are surfaced in the grid's
VoiceOver summary so the `online` i18n key stays live and the data is conveyed without a visible
row — enriching accessibility while keeping the visible grid identical to the web.

